@api = https://localhost:7201
# An access token from auth carrying each request's scope, for example one a registered API application gets with
# client credentials. Agents don't use this file: they authenticate with their certificate.
@token = <access token>

### Create a tenant under a parent (only a Superadministrator creates a root tenant, without parentTenantId)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Contoso",
  "contactEmail": "it@contoso.example",
  "parentTenantId": "<parent tenant id>",
  "maxDevices": 25
}

### List tenants
GET {{api}}/api/v1/tenants?page=1&pageSize=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a tenant's fields (JSON merge patch: send only what changes; null clears)
PATCH {{api}}/api/v1/tenants/<tenant id>
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json

{
  "maxDevices": 50
}

### Suspend a tenant (then :activate or :cancel)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/tenants/<tenant id>:suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Issue an enrollment token: its secret is in this response only. Run the agent with it to enroll a machine.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/tenants/<tenant id>/enrollment-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Head office installer",
  "maxUses": 10
}

### List online devices
GET {{api}}/api/v1/devices?status=Online
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Collect a device's system info
POST {{api}}/api/v1/devices/<device id>/commands
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "CollectSystemInfo"
}
